      "review": {
        "upstream_changes": "Signed stable 6.7.5; preserve Plasma::Activities public target, SONAME 7, Ubuntu symbols, CLI and QML APIs. C++20; Ubuntu Qt >=6.10, Frameworks >=6.26.",
        "packaging_changes": "Preserve six Ubuntu binaries and Multi-Arch metadata. Remove unused KF6WindowSystem/xkbcommon and obsolete Doxygen Build-Depends after complete signed source review. QDoc replaced BUILD_QCH upstream; retain a documentation package containing the explicit common optional documentation profile, with real QCH generation still a separate gate.",
        "build_dependencies": "Exact ECM/KConfig/KCoreAddons retained version and hash closure (13 binaries), eligible under their original Frameworks evidence scope. Retain Ubuntu Qt and Boost; bare clean sbuild certifies dependency sufficiency.",
        "test_policy": "Require upstream registered QFlatSetTest. Non-registered PlasmaActivitiesTest ignores qExec failures and is not inferred PASS from exit status. Before compilation, run an Ubuntu SDK client with offline behavior and the actual isolated Ubuntu kactivitymanagerd: create/rename/select/remove futures/signals, C++ model, installed QML plugin and CLI. Upgrade all six binaries and re-run the unchanged client, then rebuild and re-run the consumer. All failures report the check.",
        "activation_policy": "Private D-Bus and temporary XDG config/data/cache/state/runtime; offscreen Qt. Only owned daemon PID is terminated. Ubuntu daemon and Qt versions must remain unchanged; whole-desktop integration remains a later gate.",
        "frameworks_revalidation": "KConfig packaging-only revision 6.30.0-0supralinux5 passed authoritative KVM compilation, 90 upstream tests, source/binary lintian and Ubuntu/retained-Supra upgrades. Use its exact reviewed binaries; certify the new combined cache transport before a new Activities Attempt."
